WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.929
Daily Practice Checklist.

2
00:00:02.209 --> 00:00:04.662
From the Reference part of the Soft Skill Playbook.

3
00:00:06.412 --> 00:00:07.436
The key idea.

4
00:00:07.716 --> 00:00:10.873
Ten minutes a day beats a two-hour workshop once a year.

5
00:00:11.153 --> 00:00:12.625
Print this page or pin it.

6
00:00:13.975 --> 00:00:14.829
Part 1.

7
00:00:15.109 --> 00:00:16.495
Every day (10 minutes).

8
00:00:17.745 --> 00:00:19.687
Speak at least once in every meeting.

9
00:00:19.967 --> 00:00:22.185
Put the main point first in every message.

10
00:00:22.465 --> 00:00:25.153
Rewrite one message to be shorter before sending.

11
00:00:25.433 --> 00:00:27.951
Learn and use one phrase from the Phrase Bank.

12
00:00:28.231 --> 00:00:31.516
One 5-minute AI role-play with the Master Prompt.

13
00:00:31.796 --> 00:00:35.615
Journal 3 lines: what I said, how it landed, what I'll try next.

14
00:00:36.965 --> 00:00:37.839
Part 2.

15
00:00:38.119 --> 00:00:39.037
Every week.

16
00:00:40.287 --> 00:00:43.465
Prepare a written one-on-one agenda for your manager.

17
00:00:43.745 --> 00:00:46.177
Have one conversation outside your team.

18
00:00:46.457 --> 00:00:50.105
Record yourself for 2 minutes explaining a technical concept.

19
00:00:50.385 --> 00:00:52.796
Give specific praise to at least two people.

20
00:00:53.076 --> 00:00:58.665
Try one real-life scenario: order at a café, ask directions, small talk on a train.

21
00:01:00.015 --> 00:01:00.911
Part 3.

22
00:01:01.191 --> 00:01:02.109
Every month.

23
00:01:03.359 --> 00:01:04.895
Redo the self-assessment.

24
00:01:05.175 --> 00:01:08.439
Ask for feedback on your communication from one person.

25
00:01:08.719 --> 00:01:13.412
Do one visibility action: demo, presentation, write-up, knowledge-share.

26
00:01:13.692 --> 00:01:16.935
Have the one difficult conversation you've been postponing.

27
00:01:17.215 --> 00:01:18.580
Update your wins file.

28
00:01:19.930 --> 00:01:20.847
Part 4.

29
00:01:21.127 --> 00:01:23.047
Before any important conversation.

30
00:01:24.297 --> 00:01:25.215
Step 1:

31
00:01:25.495 --> 00:01:28.311
Goal: what do I want them to know or decide or do?

32
00:01:28.591 --> 00:01:29.508
Step 2:

33
00:01:29.788 --> 00:01:31.644
Audience: what do they care about?

34
00:01:31.924 --> 00:01:33.119
(altitude rule).

35
00:01:33.399 --> 00:01:34.316
Step 3:

36
00:01:34.596 --> 00:01:36.772
Headline: my point in one sentence.

37
00:01:37.052 --> 00:01:38.012
Step 4:

38
00:01:38.292 --> 00:01:39.145
Evidence:

39
00:01:39.425 --> 00:01:41.132
2 to 3 facts or numbers.

40
00:01:41.412 --> 00:01:42.372
Step 5:

41
00:01:42.652 --> 00:01:44.337
Ask: the exact next step.

42
00:01:44.617 --> 00:01:45.556
Step 6:

43
00:01:45.836 --> 00:01:46.583
Breathe:

44
00:01:46.863 --> 00:01:49.188
4 to 4-6 breathing, then go.

45
00:01:50.538 --> 00:01:52.074
That's the end of this lesson.

46
00:01:52.354 --> 00:01:57.005
Pick one script from it, say it out loud three times, and use it for real today.

47
00:01:57.285 --> 00:02:03.407
For extra practice, paste the Master Prompt into an AI assistant and role-play the conversation.

